WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.930
A headline flashes up on the screen:
ninety per cent of people exercise every

2
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.190
single day.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.420
Impressive.

4
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:09.360
Now the camera pulls back.

5
00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:13.120
The survey was done with a clipboard,
right at the door of a gym.

6
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.520
So what went wrong?

7
00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.280
Were too few people asked?

8
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.570
Or was it the wrong kind of data?

9
00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:21.100
In this mission, you'll
separate the population,

10
00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.400
the whole group you want to know about,
from the sample you actually collect data

11
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.160
from.

12
00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.340
You'll meet five sampling techniques, from
simple random to quota and convenience,

13
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.590
and decide which ones are random.

14
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.150
And you'll learn what
makes a sample biased,

15
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.740
and why that matters for any conclusion.

16
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain what
went wrong with the gym survey.
